(6183819, 912966, 40391, '<td valign="top">I really like the single colour this shot represents.  However, it''s the lighting and DoF that (as well as originality) that sets this above most other''s in this challenge.<br/> <br/>I''m not sure how I feel about the border.  It basically works because the mirrored parts are already OOF except for the LHS tensioning knob that has been split into distinct banding, which creates an unwanted distraction for me.  Overall, I really like this and it got an 8 from me.</td>', 'I really like the single colour this shot represents.  However, it''s the lighting and DoF that (as well as originality) that sets this above most other''s in this challenge. I''m not sure how I feel about the border.  It basically works because the mirrored parts are already OOF except for the LHS tensioning knob that has been split into distinct banding, which creates an unwanted distraction for me.  Overall, I really like this and it got an 8 from me.', '2010-10-06 19:08:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6183823, 913094, 40391, '<td valign="top">This is a great find and well shot.  I particularly like the similar colours of the sky with the crane and how it''s softness contrast nicely with the sharpness of your subject.  The bridge and city in the background adds extra interest to your shot.<br/> <br/>A couple of things that don''t quite work for me is the over brightness of the lights and that they are also not very sharp (did you use a sturdy tripod and locked your camera mirror?).  The shadows around the crane are a little distracting but you may not have had any control over that.  I wonder if getting in closer and down lower (shooting up the crane with more sky) may have been worth a try?<br/> <br/>I do like this and gave it an 8.</td>', 'This is a great find and well shot.  I particularly like the similar colours of the sky with the crane and how it''s softness contrast nicely with the sharpness of your subject.  The bridge and city in the background adds extra interest to your shot. A couple of things that don''t quite work for me is the over brightness of the lights and that they are also not very sharp (did you use a sturdy tripod and locked your camera mirror?).  The shadows around the crane are a little distracting but you may not have had any control over that.  I wonder if getting in closer and down lower (shooting up the crane with more sky) may have been worth a try? I do like this and gave it an 8.', '2010-10-06 19:20:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6184011, 912334, 117534, '<td valign="top">Hard to make metal artistic, but you did! In my book this is the winner! I hope you post what and how you did this because I''v worked and worked to get this feel in some of my old and rustick shots. I bow to your artistic ability! 10</td>', 'Hard to make metal artistic, but you did! In my book this is the winner! I hope you post what and how you did this because I''v worked and worked to get this feel in some of my old and rustick shots. I bow to your artistic ability! 10', '2010-10-06 22:07:57.000000', NULL, 1),
